  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the skewness of the lotteries, specifically favoring the one more heavily weighted toward unfavorable outcomes (more right-skewed). Lottery B is more right-skewed, so the reason would choose B. However, the individual's reasoning focuses on maximizing the chance of 'no minus', which aligns with preferring higher probability of 0, i.e., favoring Lottery A. This is the opposite of what the skewness reason would recommend. Moreover, the individual does not consider the full distributional shape or the relative weighting of unfavorable vs. favorable outcomes in a way that reflects skewness. Instead, the focus is narrowly on the probability of avoiding loss. There is no indication that the individual assessed which lottery has more probability on unfavorable outcomes or compared the distributions in terms of skew. The reasoning is outcome-avoidance based, not distribution-shape based.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
